WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.397
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.697 --> 00:00:09.188
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.488 --> 00:00:14.984
Unit thirty: Countable and Uncountable Nouns. Today you will decide when to use many and much.

4
00:00:15.284 --> 00:00:18.146
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.402
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:24.239
Countable.

7
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:28.271
Countable means something that we can count one by one.

8
00:00:28.883 --> 00:00:30.291
Apples are countable.

9
00:00:30.883 --> 00:00:33.315
Your turn. Say: Countable.

10
00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:37.145
Countable.

11
00:00:37.883 --> 00:00:38.989
Uncountable.

12
00:00:39.983 --> 00:00:43.202
Uncountable means something that we cannot count one by one.

13
00:00:43.817 --> 00:00:45.271
Water is uncountable.

14
00:00:45.883 --> 00:00:48.501
Your turn. Say: Uncountable.

15
00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:52.507
Uncountable.

16
00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:53.996
Many.

17
00:00:54.983 --> 00:00:57.761
Many means a large number of countable things.

18
00:00:58.350 --> 00:00:59.734
There are many books.

19
00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:03.118
Your turn. Say: Many.

20
00:01:05.967 --> 00:01:06.817
Many.

21
00:01:07.583 --> 00:01:08.410
Much.

22
00:01:09.417 --> 00:01:12.066
Much means a large amount of uncountable things.

23
00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:14.092
I don't have much time.

24
00:01:14.683 --> 00:01:17.475
Your turn. Say: Much.

25
00:01:20.333 --> 00:01:21.137
Much.

26
00:01:21.883 --> 00:01:22.792
Water.

27
00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:26.247
Water means the clear liquid that we drink.

28
00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:28.107
Drink a lot of water.

29
00:01:28.717 --> 00:01:30.684
Your turn. Say: Water.

30
00:01:33.533 --> 00:01:34.314
Water.

31
00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:35.912
Rice.

32
00:01:36.917 --> 00:01:39.857
Rice means small white grains that we cook and eat.

33
00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:41.776
We eat rice every day.

34
00:01:42.383 --> 00:01:44.525
Your turn. Say: Rice.

35
00:01:47.367 --> 00:01:48.298
Rice.

36
00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:50.005
Apples.

37
00:01:51.017 --> 00:01:53.678
Apples means round fruits that grow on trees.

38
00:01:54.283 --> 00:01:55.911
I bought five apples.

39
00:01:56.517 --> 00:01:59.146
Your turn. Say: Apples.

40
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:03.013
Apples.

41
00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:04.623
A lot of.

42
00:02:05.617 --> 00:02:08.893
A lot of means a large number or amount of something.

43
00:02:09.483 --> 00:02:10.984
She has a lot of friends.

44
00:02:11.583 --> 00:02:14.526
Your turn. Say: A lot of.

45
00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:18.345
A lot of.

46
00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:23.086
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:27.160
Visal, can you count apples? Can you count water?

48
00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:37.743
We can count apples: one apple, two apples. We cannot count water in the same way. So apples are countable and water is uncountable.

49
00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:40.432
How do many and much work?

50
00:02:41.517 --> 00:02:55.308
Many is for countable nouns: many apples. Much is for uncountable nouns: much water. We use them mostly in questions and negatives: How many apples? I don't have much time.

51
00:02:56.417 --> 00:02:58.370
What about positive sentences?

52
00:02:59.483 --> 00:03:09.882
In a positive sentence, we usually use a lot of with both: There are a lot of apples. I drink a lot of water. Uncountable nouns have no plural.

53
00:03:11.033 --> 00:03:12.534
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:13.383 --> 00:03:16.300
Grammar focus: Many and much and a lot of.

55
00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:17.822
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:18.517 --> 00:03:20.075
many apples (countable)

57
00:03:20.983 --> 00:03:22.774
much water (uncountable)

58
00:03:23.683 --> 00:03:25.636
a lot of rice (both types)

59
00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:34.837
Use many with countable nouns and much with uncountable nouns, mostly in questions and negatives. Use a lot of in positive sentences with both.

60
00:03:35.583 --> 00:03:38.909
Be careful! Don't say: There are much books here.

61
00:03:40.867 --> 00:03:42.994
Say: There are many books here.

62
00:03:43.294 --> 00:03:45.352
Use many with countable nouns.

63
00:03:46.167 --> 00:03:48.540
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:49.333 --> 00:03:50.543
Counting Things.

65
00:03:50.843 --> 00:03:53.609
I have many friends, but I don't have much free time.

66
00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.460
How many apples are in the basket?

67
00:03:57.467 --> 00:04:00.023
There is a lot of rice, but there isn't much water.

68
00:04:01.033 --> 00:04:03.637
We can count apples, but we cannot count water.

69
00:04:04.633 --> 00:04:08.049
Rice and water are uncountable, so they have no plural.

70
00:04:09.133 --> 00:04:13.344
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:14.183 --> 00:04:15.811
How blank apples do you have?

72
00:04:16.111 --> 00:04:19.196
A, much. B, many. C, a lot.

73
00:04:22.733 --> 00:04:25.012
The answer is B: many.

74
00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:27.627
I don't have blank time.

75
00:04:27.927 --> 00:04:30.745
A, much. B, many. C, few.

76
00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:36.114
The answer is A: much.

77
00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:38.890
Which noun is uncountable?

78
00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:42.274
A, apple. B, book. C, rice.

79
00:04:45.833 --> 00:04:47.868
The answer is C: rice.

80
00:04:49.017 --> 00:04:50.621
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:50.921 --> 00:04:55.864
A, There are much books.. B, There are many books.. C, There is many books..

82
00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:02.061
The answer is B: There are many books..

83
00:05:03.217 --> 00:05:05.739
According to the reading, what has no plural?

84
00:05:06.039 --> 00:05:09.843
A, uncountable nouns. B, friends. C, apples.

85
00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:15.783
The answer is A: uncountable nouns.

86
00:05:16.967 --> 00:05:20.165
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:21.017 --> 00:05:23.550
Write one sentence with 'many' and one with 'much'.

88
00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:33.850
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:34.150 --> 00:05:44.935
I have many books in my room. I don't have much money in my bag. I use many with books because I can count them. I use much with money because it is uncountable in this sentence.

90
00:05:45.235 --> 00:05:46.967
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:47.883 --> 00:05:52.196
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and many and much and a lot of.

92
00:05:52.496 --> 00:05:56.507
Today's value is precision. Choose your words and numbers with care.

93
00:05:56.807 --> 00:05:59.738
See you in Unit thirty-one. Goodbye!

94
00:06:00.038 --> 00:06:03.630
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

